From: Alex Scotti <alexscotti@gmail.com>
Subject: video: frame-packed MVC - VD2 reads its eye linearly, not through AFBC

3D Blu-ray MVC played as HDMI frame packing on an AM9 Pro (S6) showed the
second eye black - on the TV, the bottom half of the packed frame - for a
whole boot, every title, until a power cycle (2026-10-25 and 2026-10-29).
Every VPP blend, window, MIF and Dolby Vision path register read the same as
on a good boot, and swapping the decoder's views left the same eye black, so
the fault was in VD2's fetch, not the stream.

On T7/S6 bits 13-14 of a layer's VDx_AFBCDM_VDTOP_CTRL0 select its source:
0 linear MIF, 1/3 the AFBC decoder (2K/4K line RAM). VD1 read 0x1200; VD2
read 0x7200 - AFBC with the 4K RAM, left there by the last thing that used
VD2 compressed, a Dolby Vision enhancement layer. For MVC, vd1_set_dcu()
programs VD2's MIF itself (its is_mvc writes) and never runs vdx_set_dcu(),
the only place VD2's select is put back to linear. So VD2 kept feeding from
an idle AFBC decoder. Writing 0x1200 to VD2_AFBCDM_VDTOP_CTRL0 by hand
during playback brought the second eye back at once.

Clear VD2's select in vd1_set_dcu() whenever it programs VD2 for MVC.
---
--- a/drivers/media/video_sink/video_hw.c
+++ b/drivers/media/video_sink/video_hw.c
@@ -2396,10 +2396,23 @@
 	}
 
 	if (cur_dev->display_module == T7_DISPLAY_MODULE ||
-		is_meson_s6_cpu())
+		is_meson_s6_cpu()) {
 		cur_dev->rdma_func[vpp_index].rdma_wr_bits
 			(vd_afbc_reg->afbc_top_ctrl,
 			0, 13, 2);
+		/*
+		 * MVC: VD2 carries the second eye, and this function programs
+		 * VD2's MIF for it (the is_mvc writes below), never vdx_set_dcu.
+		 * VD2's AFBC/MIF select has to follow, or whatever last used VD2
+		 * compressed - a Dolby Vision enhancement layer - leaves it on
+		 * the AFBC decoder (bits 13-14 = 3) and VD2 shows nothing: the
+		 * second eye of frame-packed 3D black until a power cycle.
+		 */
+		if (is_mvc)
+			cur_dev->rdma_func[vpp_index].rdma_wr_bits
+				(vd_layer[1].vd_afbc_reg.afbc_top_ctrl,
+				0, 13, 2);
+	}
 
 	/* vd mif burst len is 2 as default */
 	burst_len = 2;
